# Tú Cà Phê CRM runs on Cloudflare Workers (via @opennextjs/cloudflare),
# NOT on a traditional Node server — so it does not read a `.env` file at
# runtime in production. This file documents every environment
# variable/secret the app needs and where each one actually lives:
#
#   - Local dev secrets  -> copy .dev.vars.example to .dev.vars
#                           (read by `wrangler dev` / `next dev`)
#   - Local dev bindings -> configured in wrangler.jsonc (D1, local
#                           simulated automatically, no values needed here)
#   - Production secrets -> `wrangler secret put <NAME>` (never stored in
#                           a file at all)
#   - Production bindings/vars -> wrangler.jsonc `d1_databases`, `vars`
#                           (real IDs, not secret)
#
# See DEPLOY.md for the exact commands.

# --- Secrets (wrangler secret put / .dev.vars) ---

# One-time bootstrap token required by POST /api/setup/admin to create the
# FIRST admin account. After the first admin exists this endpoint refuses
# all further calls regardless of token, so it is safe to leave configured.
ADMIN_SETUP_TOKEN=

# Optional: Lark (Feishu) group custom-bot webhook for task-assignment
# notifications. Unset = notifications stay in-app only, no error.
LARK_WEBHOOK_URL=
LARK_SECRET=

# --- Vars (wrangler.jsonc `vars`, not secret) ---

# APP_ENV=production
# APP_NAME=Tú Cà Phê CRM

# --- Bindings (wrangler.jsonc, real resource IDs — not secret, but only
#     known after you run `wrangler d1 create`) ---
# DB               -> d1_databases[0].database_id
